From 259262bb8d810e2d9f79d91e23d58d649a097350 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:51:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): no console window on Windows double-click

GUI-subsystem exe plus AttachConsole(parent) so terminal launches keep logging.

Fixes #1278

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/ui/src/main.rs                     | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 docs/decisions/1278-windows-no-console.md | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 docs/decisions/1278-windows-no-console.md

diff --git a/crates/ui/src/main.rs b/crates/ui/src/main.rs
index 9a8e0d506..9e04a7101 100644
--- a/crates/ui/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/ui/src/main.rs
@@ -1,4 +1,28 @@
+// GUI entry point. Windows: built as a GUI-subsystem exe so a double-click opens
+// no console window (#1278); see attach_parent_console. Spec: Microsoft's public
+// documentation of the PE subsystem flag and AttachConsole.
+#![cfg_attr(windows, windows_subsystem = "windows")]
+
+/// A GUI-subsystem exe starts with no console, so launched from a terminal its
+/// stdout/stderr (tracing logs) would go nowhere. Attach to the parent's console
+/// when there is one; with none (double-click) the call just fails and is ignored.
+#[cfg(windows)]
+fn attach_parent_console() {
+    const ATTACH_PARENT_PROCESS: u32 = u32::MAX;
+    #[link(name = "kernel32")]
+    unsafe extern "system" {
+        fn AttachConsole(process_id: u32) -> i32;
+    }
+    // SAFETY: AttachConsole takes a plain integer, touches no Rust memory, and
+    // reports failure by return value, which is deliberately ignored.
+    let _ = unsafe { AttachConsole(ATTACH_PARENT_PROCESS) };
+}
+
+#[cfg(not(windows))]
+fn attach_parent_console() {}
+
 fn main() {
+    attach_parent_console();
     camcraft_app::logging::init();
     let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().skip(1).collect();
     std::process::exit(camcraft_ui::run(&args));
diff --git a/docs/decisions/1278-windows-no-console.md b/docs/decisions/1278-windows-no-console.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..69f0c35fe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/1278-windows-no-console.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# 1278 - Windows: no console window on double-click
+
+- **Chosen:** `#![cfg_attr(windows, windows_subsystem = "windows")]` on
+  `crates/ui/src/main.rs`, in debug and release alike, plus `AttachConsole(ATTACH_PARENT_PROCESS)`
+  at the top of `main` so a terminal launch still shows stdout/stderr logging.
+- **Why always, not release-only:** one behaviour on every build; a debug build run from
+  a terminal still logs there through the attach. Failure of the attach (double-click) is ignored.
+- **FFI instead of windows-sys:** windows-sys is only a transitive dependency; using it
+  directly means a new Cargo.toml dependency with feature flags (maintainer decision). A
+  single `extern "system"` declaration for kernel32 needs none. The only `unsafe` is that call.
+- **Dropped:** `AllocConsole` fallback or a file log when no console exists (out of scope;
+  tracing keeps writing to a stderr that is simply closed). The CLI binary stays a console app.

From 95005b14544e3f03f73eb465054d9cbb1f7de0b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:55:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(ui): console std handles after attach; error box with
 no console

Review of PR #1287: after a successful AttachConsole, point each NULL or
invalid stdout/stderr handle at CONOUT$ (valid ones - redirects, pipes -
are left alone), so std::io::stderr (tracing) reaches the terminal. With no
console attached, show a MessageBoxW when run returns non-zero and from a
panic hook chained after the previous one (one box per process). All new
code is cfg(windows) in crates/ui/src/win_console.rs, via extern "system"
declarations (no new dependency). Log file with no console: #1323.

Refs #1278

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
